      "imageURLs": [],
      "internal": false,
      "mergeID": "5c5907749d125f783474fdc2",
      "mergedPostDetails": "If you go into your main drive and go to \"User < appdata < locallow < VRChat\" and inspect the \"HTTPCache-WindowsPlayer\" folder you can see that vrchat takes quite a lot of space in. I think we should have an option to install the downloaded (world and avatar) data on an alternative drive (or VRChat as a whole. \n\nIn my case i only have a small ssd as my main drive and im sure im not the only one. Wiping it everytime is also a pain because than i have to redownloaded avatars/worlds which can also take time.",
